{"bill":{"id":"119-hr-9948","congress":119,"billType":"hr","billNumber":"9948","title":"To direct the President to establish an interagency task force to review, and provide recommendations on, the impact of addictive design features on youth mental health, to direct the Secretary of Health and Human Services to establish grant programs to support the activities of the task force, and for other purposes.","introducedDate":"2026-07-27","latestActionDate":"2026-07-27","latestActionText":"Referred to the Committee on Energy and Commerce, and in addition to the Committee on Education and Workforce, for a period to be subsequently determined by the Speaker, in each case for consideration of such provisions as fall within the jurisdiction of the committee concerned.","subjects":[],"sponsorBioguideId":"B001318","cosponsorBioguideIds":["D000530","S001201","W000822"],"committeeCodes":[],"committeeNames":[],"congressDotGovUrl":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/9948","source":"congress","sourceUrl":"https://www.govinfo.gov/bulkdata/BILLSTATUS/119/hr/BILLSTATUS-119hr9948.xml","fetchedAt":"2026-07-29T01:29:43.472Z"},"classification":{"billId":"119-hr-9948","plainSummary":"This bill would require the President to create a task force of federal agencies to study how design features in digital products affect young people's mental health and to recommend policy responses. The Department of Health and Human Services would award grants to support the task force's work. The bill does not itself impose new regulations on companies or change existing law governing digital platforms.","industries":[{"industry":"tech","confidence":0.85,"rationale":"The task force would examine addictive design features in digital products, which are created and deployed by technology platforms and software companies."},{"industry":"health-providers","confidence":0.4,"rationale":"The bill focuses on youth mental health impacts and directs HHS to fund related activities, which may involve health providers in research or service delivery."}],"method":"llm","model":"claude-sonnet-4-5","inputHash":"84e01c13056e3b848816d693","classifiedAt":"2026-07-30T02:14:18.941Z"},"plain":{"whatItDoes":"No one has written a summary of this bill yet. All we have is its title, and a title is not a description of a law. To find out what it does, you have to open the bill itself.","whoItTouches":"We cannot tell from the labels on this bill who it reaches. The subject is too broad to say.","everydayEffect":"Nothing has changed yet. The title alone does not say what would change for you, and this tool will not guess. Most bills never become law.","confidence":"title-only","source":"From the bill title, and from the subject labels that library staff put on it. There is no official summary of this bill yet.","titleInPlainWords":"Would direct the President to establish an interagency task force to review, and provide recommendations on, the impact of addictive design features on youth mental health, to direct the head of the federal health department to establish grant programs to support the activities of the task force."},"overlaps":[{"billId":"119-hr-9948","bioguideId":"S001201","cycle":2026,"score":0.01688580091533545,"matches":[{"industry":"health-providers","donorAmount":128500,"donorShare":0.03586488293587777,"billConfidence":0.4,"contribution":0.011476762539480887},{"industry":"tech","donorAmount":28500,"donorShare":0.007954468199786121,"billConfidence":0.85,"contribution":0.005409038375854562}],"method":{"formula":"score = Σ_industries ( donorShare(industry) × billWeight(industry) ), where billWeight = classifierConfidence / Σ classifierConfidence. Range 0–1, read as a weighted share of disclosed itemized money.","donorProfileCycle":2026,"billClassificationMethod":"llm","unclassifiedDonorShare":0.6500594991430303},"member":{"name":"Thomas R. Suozzi","chamber":"House","state":"NY","district":"3","imageUrl":"data/portraits/S001201.jpg","role":"Cosponsor"},"donorPro